THIS LICENCE COVERS THE CODE ONLY. IT DOES NOT AND CANNOT COVER THE DATA.

None of the data this repository fetches belongs to its author, so none of it is
licensed here. What follows is what was checked, so that a downstream user knows
which terms apply to what. The authoritative quotes, with URLs, are in the
docstring of each module under sources/.

  CFTC Commitments of Traders (cftc_*)
      A publication of the U.S. Commodity Futures Trading Commission. US
      Government work, public domain. Freely usable and redistributable.

  Daily closes (prices)
      Yahoo Finance's chart endpoint. Not a documented public API; subject to
      Yahoo's terms of service. Used here at low volume for personal research.
      This repository redistributes none of it.

  OpenRouter model pricing (openrouter_pricing)
      OpenRouter's public models endpoint. The committed CSVs under
      data/snapshots/openrouter_pricing/ are the only data files in this
      repository, and they are published prices rather than proprietary figures.

  University of Michigan Surveys of Consumers (umich_sca)
      NOT redistributed here, deliberately and by construction. The University
      of Michigan grants permission-free USE of the tables published on its
      public site and separately prohibits redistribution without express
      written consent. This repository fetches these tables into a local,
      version-control-excluded database and charts them; it commits no copy of
      them, and the test fixture's slice of this source is fabricated rather
      than sampled. Attribution, as the University requests:

          University of Michigan, Survey Research Center, Surveys of Consumers.

If you add a source, record its terms on the Source declaration. A source marked
redistributable=False is forbidden by the test suite from having any committed
artefact, which is what keeps this section true rather than aspirational.
